# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ExamSmasher — environment
#
# Everything works with NOTHING configured. Copy this file to `.env.local`
# only if you want the two optional upgrades:
#
#   - syllabus analysis, papers, notes, quiz, plans -> rule-based engine
#     (always available, honest, built only from your syllabus)
#   - syllabus files (.pdf/.docx/.txt/photo)        -> read by the one
#     server route, `POST /api/extract`, using local parsers + Tesseract OCR
#   - the optional in-browser model                 -> downloaded from
#     Hugging Face on first use and cached by the browser (used only when
#     no server-side key is set)
#
# OPTIONAL — real per-topic YouTube video discovery (server-side only):
#
#   YOUTUBE_API_KEY=...
#
#   Without it, each topic falls back to honest YouTube SEARCH LINKS (the
#   UI says why). With it, `POST /api/videos` returns real titles, channels,
#   durations, view counts and thumbnails — the key never reaches the
#   browser. Each search costs 100 quota units (default 10,000/day), so
#   results are cached on both server and client.
#
# OPTIONAL — AI-written study notes (server-side only):
#
#   GEMINI_API_KEY=...
#   LLM_MODEL=gemini-3.5-flash-lite     # optional override; this is the default
#
#   Without it, notes come from the in-browser model (if loaded) or the rule
#   engine — the panel footer always says which one actually wrote them.
#   With it, `POST /api/notes` writes the full 12-element structure with a
#   server-side model; the key never reaches the browser. `LLM_MODEL` must
#   be a model name that works on your key (the default is verified to).
#
# SECURITY: keys in `.env.local` are read by server routes ONLY. Never
# import them in client components (`"use client"` files). The file itself
# is ignored by git either way.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
